Four things the executable form had to resolve, because the draft is prose:

1. Patch 1c (the stub-chain footnote) is NOT carried. It is conditional on the
   Sepolia rehearsal not having run — a claim about the world that no artifact
   in this repository can verify, and one the runbook keeps or deletes by hand.

2. Patches 1a and 1b target the SAME §3 bullet: 1b rewrites it, while 1a's
   instruction ("insert after ... or use the direct calldata path.") quotes the
   pre-1b text. They compose as 1b's rewrite followed by 1a's two new bullets —
   the only reading under which both instructions hold.

3. Patch 4b quotes "…rather than silently underpaying." That phrase lived in
   the pre-flip "v0.9.0 must do" item 4, which doc-flips Patch 6h.7 replaced, so
   the sentence lands at the end of the post-flip item 4. The residual tense
   mismatch ("a separate release-prep deliverable" immediately followed by
   "Landed in v0.9.0") is left VISIBLE for the human: item 4 is not a
   gate-checked line, and inventing replacement prose is not this file's job.

4. Patch 4a replaces doc-flips 6h.7's unchecked fee box verbatim; the checked
   block is the draft's, unchanged.

Placeholders remain by design: <<EST-*>> (measured numbers, from the
deployment-day `spore contract estimate` output) plus <<ADDR>> and <<DEPLOYER>>
(the flip's receipt values). Fill them from the receipt and the saved estimator
output BEFORE applying; this file is the shape, not the measurement.

The drafts' own completion criterion (`grep -n 'FILL' docs/LIVE_NODES.md ...`
returns no hits) is already non-zero on the pre-flip tree — LIVE_NODES §3's tag
instructions read "search for the FILL markers" — so key on the placeholder
SHAPE (`<<EST-`, `<<ADDR>>`, `<<DEPLOYER>>`, `<release>`) instead. The
rehearsal reports the outstanding ones.
